    "memo": "BILL NUMBER:S2160A\n\nTITLE OF BILL:\nAn act\nto amend the highway law, in relation to the designation of the\n\"Saratoga County Veterans' Memorial Highway\"\n\nPURPOSE:\nThis bill will designate a portion of state highway route 29.\nstarting at 61 Lake Avenue,\nSaratoga Springs. running along state route 29 east to\nroute 4 in the village of Schuylerville (Town of Saratoga) south on\nroute 4, past the Saratoga National Cemetery and the\nSaratoga Battlefield, through the Town of Stillwater into the City of\nMechanicville into the Town of Waterford and ending at the Saratoga\nCounty line in Waterford on route 4 as Saratoga County Veterans'\nMemorial Highway.\n\nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\nSection one- amends the highway law by adding a new section 342-kkk\ndesignates a portion of state highway route 29, starting at 61 Lake\nAvenue, Saratoga Springs, running along state route 29 east to route\n4 in the Village of Schuylerville (Town of Saratoga) south on route 4.\npast the Saratoga National cemetery and the Saratoga Battlefield,\nthrough the Town of Stillwater into the city of Mechanicville into\nthe Town of Waterford end ending at the Saratoga County line in\nWaterford on route 4 as Saratoga County Veterans' Memorial Highway.\n\nSection two- calls for the commissioner of transportation to provide\nfor the installation and maintenance of adequate signing of the state\nhighway system as designated pursuant to section one of this act.\n\nSection three - Effective date.\n\nJUSTIFICATION:\nSaratoga County Board of Supervisors Veterans' Committee passed a\nmotion for Saratoga County Veterans' Memorial Highway to start at the\nNew York State Military museum at 61 Lake Avenue Saratoga Springs, NY\n(state Route 29). East to State Route 4 in Schuylerville, NY Town of\nSaratoga south on route 4, past the Saratoga National Cemetery and\nthe Saratoga Battlefield, through the Town of Stillwater into the\nCity of Mechanicville into the Town of Waterford and ending at the\nSaratoga County line in Waterford on route 4.\n\nVarious local V.F.W. Posts and American Legion posts have sent letters\nof support for the designation of the Saratoga County Veterans'\nMemorial Highway. This bill would increase the visibility of the\nhistoric corridor in  Saratoga County which was the location of\nthe Battle of Saratoga\n\"Turning point of the Revolutionary War\". This would also benefit the\nSaratoga National Cemetery and the New York state Military Museum.\n\nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\nNew Bill.\n\nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\nNone to the state.\n\n\nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n\n",
