    "lawCode": "Add §342-iii, Hway L",
    "lawSection": "Highway Law",
    "memo": "BILL NUMBER:S2160B\n\nTITLE OF BILL:\nAn act\nto amend the highway law, in relation to the designation of the\n\"Saratoga County Veterans' Memorial Highway\"\n\nPURPOSE:\nPortion of the state highway system to be designated as the \"Saratoga\nCounty Veterans' Memorial Highway\". That portion of state highway\nroute 32 in Waterford north to its intersection with route 423 in the\nTown of Stillwater then continuing both: (a) north along route 32\npast the Saratoga National Cemetery and the Saratoga Battlefield to\nWilbur Road in the Town of Saratoga;\nand (b) east along route 423 in the Town of Stillwater to route 9P\nnorth in the Town of Saratoga and ending at the route 9p bridge over\nFish Creek in the Town of Saratoga shall be designated as the\n\"Saratoga County Veterans' Memorial Highway\".\n\nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\nSection one- amends the highway law by adding a new section 342-iii\nDesignates Portion of the state highway system to be designated as\nthe \"Saratoga County Veterans' Memorial Highway\". That portion of\nstate highway route 32 in Waterford north to its intersection with\nroute 423 in the Town of Stillwater then continuing both: (a) north\nalong route 32 past the Saratoga National Cemetery and the Saratoga\nBattlefield to Wilbur Road in the Town of Saratoga; and (b) east\nalong route 423 in the Town of Stillwater to route 9P north in the\nTown of Saratoga and ending at the route 9p bridge over Fish Creek in\nthe Town of Saratoga shall be designated as the \"Saratoga County\nVeterans' Memorial Highway\".\n\nSection two- calls for the commissioner of transportation to provide\nfor the installation and maintenance of adequate signing of the state\nhighway system as designated pursuant to section one of this act.\n\nSection three - Effective date.\n\nJUSTIFICATION:\nSaratoga County Board of Supervisors Veterans' Committee passed a\nmotion for Saratoga County Veterans' Memorial Highway to start at the\nNew York State Military museum at 61 Lake Avenue Saratoga Springs, NY\n(state Route 29). East to State Route 4 in Schuylerville, NY Town of\nSaratoga south on route 4, past the Saratoga National Cemetery and\nthe Saratoga Battlefield, through the Town of Stillwater into the\nCity of Mechanicville into the Town of Waterford and ending at the\nSaratoga County line in Waterford on route 4.\n\nVarious local V.F.W. Posts and American Legion posts have sent letters\nof support for the designation of the Saratoga County Veterans'\nMemorial Highway. This bill would increase the visibility of the\nhistoric corridor in Saratoga County which was the location of the\nBattle of Saratoga \"Turning point of the Revolutionary War\". This\nwould also benefit the Saratoga National Cemetery and the New York\nstate Military Museum.\n\n\nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\nNew Bill.\n\nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\nNone to the state.\n\nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n\n",
